<title>UK: Britt Allcroft shares set debut premium.</title>
<headline>Britt Allcroft shares set debut premium.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Britt Allcroft Plc set a 22.6 percent premium on their first day of trading on the London Stock Exchange on Wednesday.</p>
<p>By 1100 GMT the shares were quoted at 159-1/2p, setting a strong premium to the placing price of 130p. Trading volume was 877,300 shares.</p>
<p>The company, which holds the television, video and character licensing rights to Thomas the Tank Engine &amp; Friends, had a market capitalisation of 30.6 million stg at the offer price.</p>
<p>-- John Sutherland, London Newsroom +44 171 542 7945</p>
</text>
